# Guessing Game - Docker Guide

A simple guessing game application that can be easily run using Docker.

## Prerequisites

- Docker installed on your system
- Docker running in the background

## Building the Docker Image

To build the Docker image for this application, run:

```bash
docker build -t guessing-game .
```

This command builds an image named `guessing-game` using the Dockerfile in the project directory.

## Running the Container

To run the guessing game in a Docker container:

```bash
docker run -p 5000:5000 guessing-game
```

This will:
- Start a container from the `guessing-game` image
- Map port 5000 from the container to port 5000 on your local machine
- The game will be accessible at `http://localhost:5000`

## Stopping the Container

To stop a running container, press `Ctrl+C` in the terminal where it's running, or use:

```bash
docker stop <container_id>
```

## Project Structure

- `main/server/app.py` - Main Flask application
- `main/business/business_service.py` - Game logic
- `main/presentation/index.html` - Web interface
- `requirements.txt` - Python dependencies
- `Dockerfile` - Docker configuration

## Troubleshooting

If port 5000 is already in use, you can map to a different port:

```bash
docker run -p 8000:5000 guessing-game
```

Then access the game at `http://localhost:8000`
